+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value |
+| ------ | ----- |
+| Issue  | #37   |
+| Status | Draft |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before the executor runs. A rejection is returned as a `ToolResponse`, never thrown, so the model can read it and correct the call; only an unknown tool name throws.
+
+## Behaviour
+
+- Input missing a required property is rejected with a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the property, and the executor is never invoked. ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property without running the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L19))
+- A wrong-typed property is rejected with a message naming the property path and the expected type, and neither the returned text nor any log line contains the offending value. ([validated by: names the path and expected type of a wrong-typed field but never its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L31))
+- Registering a tool whose schema cannot be compiled throws at registration, and the message names the tool. ([validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when its schema cannot compile](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L55))
+- A function-valued tool definition is validated against the schema it returns at that call, not a stale cached one. ([validated by: validates a function-valued definition against the schema current at each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L61))
